  "instructions": [
    "Edit names and details here. Keep employeeId, department code, account key and student rollNo stable: they identify existing records. For staff account username changes, matchEmail must be the current database login and email is the desired new login; refresh matchEmail to the current login before a later username change.",
    "After saving this file, stop the running app with Ctrl+C and run npm.cmd run college:update. It validates, previews, backs up local MySQL, builds, imports and starts the app automatically.",
    "The single update command gives newly created faculty demo accounts password123 unless COLLEGE_IMPORT_PASSWORD is already set. Existing passwords and account activation states are preserved. Never put SMTP, database, AWS credentials or private passwords in this file.",
    "The import updates listed records only; removing an entry does not delete or archive a database record. Register new students through Student Registration first, then add their roll numbers here.",
    "The single update command rebuilds and restarts the application so branding and demo login changes are picked up. This file is bundled at build time, not served publicly as a downloadable file.",
    "Student names/roll numbers were supplied by the client. Their edupilot.edu usernames are demo login IDs, not provisioned email inboxes. Academic/contact seed data and non-CSE departments remain illustrative.",
    "CSE faculty names, qualifications and designations follow the linked official directory checked on 2026-11-09. All edupilot.edu faculty logins and employee IDs are application identifiers, not official college contact details.",
    "The directory lists Dr. G. Syam Prasad as CSE HOD. Gupta is Assistant Professor there but Professor of CSE on the governing-body page; confirm his designation with the college.",
    "The principal has a separate administrator demo account and a faculty demo account so both application roles can be presented."
  ],
